// A host that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for listen
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host reads): the call binds no socket, and a
// consumer that binds the shorter name exits 0.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string listen
print "before";
listen("127.0.0.1" + chr(0) + "tail", 0);
